* 28sep2026
v 3
d {bf:easi : the Exact Affine Stone Index demand system in Stata}
d
d easi estimates the EASI demand system of Lewbel and Pendakur (2009) entirely
d within Stata and Mata: iterated restricted 3SLS with Slutsky symmetry, the
d implicit utility index, expenditure, price (compensated and uncompensated) and
d demographic elasticities of the households, the individuals or the market,
d with influence-function standard errors, sampling weights, robust, cluster,
d survey-design (svyset) and bootstrap variance; the households that do not buy
d (missing prices imputed, the Shonkwiler-Yen correction); tables with stars
d exported to Word, LaTeX, Excel, CSV or Markdown; predict, estat engel, and a
d pre-estimation diagnostic, easidiag, that detects the causes of slow or
d failed convergence before any estimation is run.  sr_easi is kept as a
d backward-compatible wrapper.
d
d Author  : {bf:Abdelkrim Araar}, Universite Laval / PEP
d Email   : {browse "mailto:aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca":aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca}
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260928
d Version       : 2.0.0 (28 September 2026)
d Stata Version : 14.2 and higher
d
d Ancillary files (net get easi): hixdata.dta, the reference data of Lewbel
d and Pendakur (2009); mex_bench.dta, a reduced Mexican expenditure survey
d (ENIGH 2014, cereals) with a stratified two-stage design already svyset;
d a guided tour on hixdata; a tour of the survey-design features on the
d Mexican data; and a script that prepares hixdata for the dialog.
d
f src/easi.ado
f src/easi_p.ado
f src/easi_estat.ado
f src/easi.sthlp
f src/easi.dlg
f src/easidiag.ado
f src/easidiag.sthlp
f src/sr_easi.ado
f src/sr_easi_estat.ado
f src/_easi_tabstars.ado
f src/_easi_pimpute.ado
f src/easi_examples.ado
